{
  "$comment": "L3 recall . One in-memory tokenizer + BM25 shared by the three clients so the same items and query give the same hits byte for byte; client FTS engines are not used. Ranking, the coverage gate, Top-K, conflict detection and resolution are fixed here; [D] rendering and the recallMax fitting live in assemble.v1. Items are memory-items.v2 inputs, canonicalised with defaults before use.",
  "schema": "oriveo.context.memory-recall",
  "version": 1,
  "dependsOn": [
    "memory-items",
    "assemble"
  ],
  "constants": {
    "k1": 1.2,
    "b": 0.75,
    "topK": 5,
    "coverageMin": 0.25,
    "minMatchedTerms": 2,
    "idfPriorDocs": 20,
    "scopeFactor": {
      "conversation": 1.2,
      "folder": 1.1,
      "global": 1
    },
    "pinnedFactor": 1.2,
    "halfLifeDays": 180,
    "timeFloor": 0.5,
    "confidenceFloor": 0.5,
    "maxQueryCodePoints": 8000,
    "conflictJaccardMin": 0.5,
    "joiners": "_.-/#",
    "cjkRanges": [
      [
        4352,
        4607
      ],
      [
        12352,
        12447
      ],
      [
        12448,
        12543
      ],
      [
        12592,
        12687
      ],
      [
        12784,
        12799
      ],
      [
        13312,
        19903
      ],
      [
        19968,
        40959
      ],
      [
        44032,
        55215
      ],
      [
        63744,
        64255
      ],
      [
        131072,
        201551
      ]
    ]
  },
  "rules": [
    "1 Normalise: NFKC, then lowercase (locale-independent), then fold ς (U+03C2) to σ; work on Unicode code points.",
    "2 Word chars = general category L*, N* or M*. A CJK char is a word char whose code point lies in a cjkRanges interval (inclusive). A maximal run of word chars splits where CJK-ness changes; a non-CJK sub-run is one token; a CJK sub-run of length 1 is that char, of length ≥ 2 its adjacent bigrams in order.",
    "3 Compound tokens, appended after all word tokens in text order: a maximal run of word chars and joiners (constants.joiners), with leading and trailing joiners stripped, that still contains a joiner, is one extra token.",
    "4 Index: only items with layer episodic, status active and at least one token; N = their count, df(t) = items containing t, avgdl = mean token count. idf(t) = ln(1 + (N + idfPriorDocs − df + 0.5)/(df + 0.5)) (idfPriorDocs empty pseudo-documents keep a few same-topic items from pushing their shared terms to idf ≈ 0). Rebuild whenever the item set changes.",
    "5 Query = the first maxQueryCodePoints code points of the fresh user message; its distinct tokens form Q. Empty Q or empty index → no hits.",
    "6 Per indexed item, in order: drop when expiresAt is set and not after now; drop when scope is not visible (global; conversation id = this conversation; folder id = this folder; ids compared lowercased). bm25 = Σ over the item's distinct terms t ∈ Q of idf(t)·tf·(k1+1)/(tf + k1·(1 − b + b·len/avgdl)); drop when bm25 ≤ 0 or fewer than min(minMatchedTerms, distinct terms of the item) of its distinct terms are in Q. coverage = round6(Σ idf of its distinct terms in Q / Σ idf of all its distinct terms); drop when coverage < coverageMin.",
    "7 score = round6(bm25 × scopeFactor[conversation|folder|global] × (pinned ? pinnedFactor : 1) × (timeFloor + (1 − timeFloor)·0.5^(ageDays/halfLifeDays)) × (confidenceFloor + (1 − confidenceFloor)·clamp(confidence, 0, 1))). time = first of occurredAt, source.observedAt, createdAt that parses as RFC 3339; ageDays = max(0, (now − time)/86400000 ms), 0 when no time. round6(x) = floor(x·1e6 + 0.5)/1e6.",
    "8 Order by score descending, then id ascending (code-unit order of the lowercase UUID); keep the first topK. A hit = {id, text: content, date: UTC YYYY-MM-DD of time or null, score, coverage}.",
    "9 Caller: only for fresh chat sends with effective useMemory on (any account, Free included: L3 is local); the hits go to assemble dynamic.recall as {id, text, date} and the same entries are reused by every leg, retry and continue of that turn. A new L3 item created locally gets occurredAt = now when none was given.",
    "10 Conflict (on saving an L3 item): against active episodic items other than itself with the same kind and the same scope (type equal, ids equal lowercased): Jaccard of distinct token sets, round6; conflict when Jaccard ≥ conflictJaccardMin and < 1 (equal sets are a duplicate). Pick the highest Jaccard, then lowest id. The caller then sets both to conflicted with conflictGroupId = the older id; conflicted items are never recalled.",
    "11 Resolve: useNew → newer active with supersedes += older id, older superseded; useOld → newer superseded, older active; keepBoth → both active. Both get conflictGroupId null; nothing is deleted. The repository writes them as ordinary local edits (L3 never syncs)."
  ],
